---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../config';

/*
  Required by the email capture (NOTES.md §7). Review this if analytics or an
  email provider get added — both change what's true below.
*/
const updated = 'July 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description={`What ${SITE_NAME} collects, which is almost nothing.`}
>
  <article class="pt-14 pb-8 sm:pt-20">
    <header class="wrap-prose">
      <h1 class="text-[2.25rem] sm:text-[3rem]">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Short, because there isn't much to say.
      </p>
      <hr class="mt-8 border-rule" />
    </header>

    <div class="wrap-prose prose-note mt-8">
      <h2>Accounts</h2>
      <p>
        There are none. Nothing on this site requires signing in, and no personal
        profile is created or stored.
      </p>

      <h2>The email list</h2>
      <p>
        If you subscribe, your email address is stored by the newsletter provider for
        the sole purpose of sending you posts. It is never sold, rented, or shared.
        Every email includes an unsubscribe link, and unsubscribing deletes the
        address. You can also ask to be removed by writing to
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Aggregate page-view counts may be collected to see which things people
        actually use. No cookies are set for this, and no attempt is made to identify
        or track individual visitors across sites.
      </p>

      <h2>The games and maps</h2>
      <p>
        They run entirely in your browser. Your picks, filters, and progress stay on
        your device and are never transmitted anywhere. Some of them save your
        progress in your browser's local storage, which you can clear at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served by a hosting provider that keeps standard server logs,
        including IP addresses, for security and abuse prevention. Fonts are served
        from this domain, not from a third party.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        Last updated {updated}. If this policy changes in a way that matters, the
        change will be noted here.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
